---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="About Alexey Timin and Systems in Practice"
	pubDate={new Date('May 29 2026')}
>
	<div class="about-intro">
		<img
			class="avatar"
			src="https://github.com/atimin.png?size=240"
			alt="Alexey Timin"
			width="160"
			height="160"
			loading="eager"
			decoding="async"
		/>

		<p>
			I'm Alexey Timin, a software engineer and the creator of <a href="https://www.reduct.store/"
				>ReductStore</a
			>, a time-series object store built for edge AI, robotics, computer vision, and industrial data.
		</p>
	</div>

	<p>
		Systems in Practice is where I write personal notes about building and using ReductStore in
		real systems. The focus is storage, edge data, deployment constraints, customer use cases, and
		the engineering decisions that only become visible when software has to run in production.
	</p>

	<p>
		I use this blog to document practical lessons rather than polished marketing stories: what worked,
		what did not, why certain trade-offs were made, and how ReductStore fits into existing systems
		without forcing teams to rebuild everything around it.
	</p>

	<p>
		You can find my code on <a href="https://github.com/atimin">GitHub</a> and connect with me on
		<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/atimin/">LinkedIn</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>

<style>
	.about-intro {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1.5rem;
		align-items: stretch;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.avatar {
		align-self: center;
		width: 160px;
		height: 160px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		box-shadow: var(--box-shadow);
	}

	.about-intro p {
		margin: 0;
	}

	@media (max-width: 560px) {
		.about-intro {
			text-align: center;
		}
	}
</style>
